From 546a0cfe26ef33a5c13b2dd7566b44bb9a9213dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: complete and deterministic savestates (run-ahead,
 rewind, netplay)

Loading a state did not give back the same game as playing on without
loading: picture of the first frame, sound sample by sample, then the
QSound Z80 timing, all differed (also on the plain arcade sfa3 driver).
Missing from the states, and now saved for the HSFA drivers only:

- QSound (qs_c.cpp): resampler position nDelta and interpolation samples.
  They decide when the chip produces its samples, hence when ready_flag
  rises for the Z80: after a load the sound driver ran on other cycles;
- CPS2 sprite list copies of the previous frames (cps_obj.cpp);
- converted palette (cps_pal.cpp): kept as the words last converted per
  page, converted again at the first draw after a load (cps_draw.cpp)
  instead of re-reading the palette RAM at that time;
- latched "F" registers CpsSaveFrg (layer / sprite shift of the next
  frame, wrong in a fresh instance);
- Cps2Volume, QSound routes set again on load (only every 5 frames before);
- Taunt on Select (patch 0014): previous Coin and pending taunt;
- secret options already written (patch 0003);
- widescreen (patches 0022 / 0023): scroll1 ring tracking and slope k. The
  tracking now runs on every frame from Cps2Frame (HsfaWsSuivi), drawn or
  not, so that the saved tracking follows the game when run-ahead skips the
  draw of the real frames; drawing every frame gives the same picture as
  before.

The data is one zone ("HSF9", version 1) at the very end of the libretro
state, after the blending registers of patch 0010, and is read only when
the loaded state holds it whole: states saved before this patch still
load (the widescreen tracking restarts), and new states load in older
cores (extra bytes ignored). HSFA_ETATS_FIN=0: no zone, states identical
to the byte to the previous core. HSFA_ETATS_SANS=<mask> (tests): parts
read but not applied on load.

Checked on the 5 games, 4:3 and 16:9 (headless libretro harness): load
then play on, simulated run-ahead (1 and 2 frames, real frame without
picture or sound), two loads in a row, load into a fresh instance:
picture, sound (sample by sample) and final state identical to the game
without load. Without loads, picture and sound identical to the previous
core on every frame.
